{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNkJ98tXRoTS86Q9dWYl","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for a private rundown of what comes next plus one batched request. The audit shows the card instance geometry is correct at 298 x 424.9 (image 298, name 27, rating row, price), so the missing card text in the Home screenshot is a sizing bug, not a content bug: naKids Grid reports h=100 while its cardInst child is 424.9 tall. The cause sits in my frame() helper. For a HORIZONTAL frame the primary axis is width, so primaryAxisSizingMode='AUTO' hugs width, and my line setting counterAxisSizingMode='FIXED' plus resize(w, n.height) pinned height at the default 100. Vertical frames hug height correctly, which is why cardInst reads 424.9 and Dress Style reads 208, but Grid, the Panel rows and the tile rows all sit at 100.\n\nThe icons are broken differently: star is 2.7 x 2.4 inside a 16 component. The ratio 2.7/17 is 0.16, i.e. 16/100, so rescale used a width of 100, meaning the resize(17,16) never took effect before rescale ran. Rather than debug that path I fix the icons in place: for each Icon/* component I take the ink bbox over its children, compute k = compWidth / inkW, then for every child apply resize(w*k, h*k) and set x=(x-minX)*k, y=(y-minY)*k. In-place repair keeps existing instances valid.\n\nFor layout I sweep every FRAME (skipping INSTANCE nodes) whose layoutMode is HORIZONTAL and whose height is exactly 100, setting counterAxisSizingMode='AUTO' so height hugs. Frames with explicit heights (Hero 660, Image 660, Main 596, the 290 tiles, Newsletter 190) stay fixed.\n\nI rebuild the Product Review Card with a nested Rating instance named \"Stars\" defaulting to Score=4.5, so per-review overrides go through swapComponent on that nested instance; Reviewer, verified, quote and date stay as text.\n\nI rebuild 03_Product and 04_Cart with the corrected helper: horizontal → primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED when o.w is given, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED only when o.h is given; vertical → primaryAxisSizingMode FIXED only when o.h is given, counterAxisSizingMode FIXED when o.w is given; resize defaults to 100 x 100 and AUTO hugs whatever is unspecified.\n\nEverything touches the same file, so one use_figma call runs icons, then the sweep, then the two screens, and a screenshot of Category (18:637) goes alongside as a read-only check.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":8539,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":188023,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":8539}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c5d4f2f-9471-4ee4-b741-5d1ccd75321e","uuid":"a4494732-05be-48ef-8b3f-10cce41e7bce","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:08:54.330Z","thinking_duration_ms":63493}
