{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-fable-5-1","id":"msg_011CgNky5Tw0GxOxKHsTA9RZ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"The user is asking for the Header, Button and Breadcrumb variant names so the component-matching regex works: the header set variants are \"=Header\" and \"=Header Shop Current\", the buttons are \"Type=Primary\" and so on, and the breadcrumb is \"=Breadcrumb Casual\". My earlier /^Header$/ fails, so the match is /^=Header$/. Home and Category share one write call to the same page to avoid a conflict, and I pair that with a read-only screenshot of the component library (9:2), since separate concurrent writes to the same Figma file risk clobbering each other. Product and Cart follow next. Variant lookup is s.children.find(c => c.name === name) with the exact names.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"output_tokens":0,"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation_input_tokens":2631,"input_tokens":55,"cache_read_input_tokens":256206,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":2631}},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c5d4f2f-9471-4ee4-b741-5d1ccd75321e","uuid":"aaac860a-ab72-4c09-8b69-b6f4aa19b8ba","timestamp":"2026-11-01T21:16:24.971Z","narration_block_indexes":[0],"thinking_duration_ms":14453}
